{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/242680-how-long-have-your-games-lasted","id":242680,"title":"How long have your games lasted?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-27T17:13:33-07:00","id":242680,"title":"How long have your games lasted?","content":"I was just wondering, how long the average game lasts. I ran a Star Trek game in the late 80s and earl 90s that went on for about four and a half years. I played in a VtM game that lasted over four years. These games were played once a week with a session lasting about 7 hrs. My current WtA game has been going on about nine months meeting every Tuesday. How often do your games meet and how long have they been running? Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T23:05:13-07:00","id":242853,"title":"","content":"My dad ran a family AD&amp;D Table Top game when I was a teen for 2 and a half years. In my 20's a helped run a werewolf Glasswalker game for 3 years online. I'm a part of a mage game and various crossovers online for the last 10 years and hopefully ongoing if RL will give me enough breaks to get writing again. The online games are sporadic, sometimes every day for a few hours online, sometimes goes for many months without a meetup or character posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:17:44-07:00","id":243045,"title":"","content":"I'm currently storytelling the 3rd year of a VTM chronicle; we play something like 2 times/month for 3-3 and half hours.<br /> strangely enough, even though 3/4 of my players changed from the first night at present, the player character are almost all the same... o__o","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:28:08-07:00","id":243053,"title":"","content":"My Mage game will be hitting its third anniversary soon as it slowly builds towards its closing chapters. I'm looking forward to running a game in a new setting to take full advantage of the experience I gained as a storyteller since starting.<br /> <br /> We'll probably pick it up every now and again to play one-shots like, &quot;What if the cabal suddenly became Nephandi? How fucked would things get?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Tall, dark, and loathsome","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2808-peryton","name":"Peryton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T06:43:57-07:00","id":243064,"title":"","content":"I was in a VTR game that lasted for about 5 years. We met every Friday from about 530pm until 10-11pm. All the players were the same. The only breaks we took were for holidays and when the Storyteller had to travel for his job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T09:50:52-07:00","id":243215,"title":"","content":"Back in university, we sometimes had two games going at a time of different systems, and alternated them by week. They generally lasted 1-2 years, and were often 2pm-11pm or so. These days we're lucky if we can game once a month, and it's more like 4pm-10pm with an hour or two of that just socializing.<br /> <br /> Then there's MUSHes. I've been on one werewolf MUSH that's run for nearly twenty years now, and still has some of its original players. I've also seen a lot of WoD places that pop up and run for somewhere between six months and two years. Fingers crossed... Anyway, the successful ones have something going most nights, and the most active players are often active many nights per week. Short scenes 1-2 hours, big events 12+ hours, but as the crowd gets older everyone tries to avoid that happening. I spent about forty hours one week in a rite of passage plotline, while also working fulltime... good times, except not. I don't think that's the norm though.<br /> <br /> Relevant <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20130613181015/http://lethaldoses.com/comics/strip18.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20130613...cs/strip18.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2214,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","user":"Traveller","date":". 08-28-2014, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T12:19:53-07:00","id":243328,"title":"","content":"My longest continuing game was about 5 years long (though technically characters -- PCs -- involved in that have continued on in other games I've run over the years, so some time can be added to that, contextually). I have a long-time friend, however, who has been running a continuing Marvel game setting (both for friends and at conventions) non-stop since 1986, or 28 years now, so I think he likely takes the prize at least out of my network of friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T14:37:56-07:00","id":243431,"title":"","content":"I'm nearing the end of a V20 Sabbat game that's run for about 3 years. I've played in another VtM game that was around 1.5 or 2 years, and a handful of oWoD stuff that was in the six month range, give or take. All of these were played with a ~5 hour session every two weeks.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I play a lot of sporatic one-shot games with different people. These cover a lot of different settings and systems, though we've run VtM and CtD. Almost half of it is Fiasco.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T06:54:35-07:00","id":243857,"title":"","content":"V:tM game that ran 13 years.<br /> I kid you not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But...we did have some seriously long gaps in between sessions, one lasting nearly 12 months so I can't claim it was a continuous spree of gaming sessions.<br /> There were months where we might have only had one game, and others where we would game every week.<br /> <br /> All in all I was glad to end it as I felt it was becoming stale.<br /> I have no plans to ever run a game that long again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T07:12:21-07:00","id":243886,"title":"","content":"One Masquerade LARP I was in was every 2 weeks (with a break for winter holidays) for about 8 years. Launched in 1996, ended shortly before NWOD began. Players would drop out for extended periods if something major happened to their character (and they wanted a break) and come back with the same character (or a new one if something happened). I went thru about 4 characters myself over that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T20:48:30-07:00","id":244484,"title":"","content":"Many of our games last maybe 6 sessions, if we're lucky. Some last just one, and others have been an ongoing setting for 20 years (with multiple characters, chronicles, and stories using the same setting and timeline.) <br /> For instance: We have a Marvel game that has been ongoing since '96-ish, where we may not play the same characters, but it's the same universe and what we did years ago still affects what happens now. The same for a game that started in '94 with the TSR module &quot;Masque of the Red Death&quot; that ran for several years with our original characters, then came to a conclusion and started again in the 1940s (with the Nazis raising Dracula and the Red Death), and then a third game (<a href=\"http://www.furnation.com/torakhan/games/masque/2k/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">Masque 2K</a>) that took place in the 2000s using the Spycraft system... where we played super-spies/agents of &quot;good-guy agents&quot; vs. &quot;bad guy vampires/undead agents&quot;. To this day, that game still crops up. At one time we had 3 GMs in 2 different states running the same setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When it comes to WoD games, most tend to only last a few sessions, unless we REALLY are attached to the game. Our latest W:tA game started in 2008, and though we've had some years in between sessions, and a few splittings of the game group, we've continued to play it when we can get enough people around.<br /> <br /> And that seems to be the issue we've ALWAYS had: Our group has always had a hard time getting the same 5-7 people in the same place, each week, at the same time. Our TSR Marvel game has over 57 &quot;active&quot; characters over the last 20 years because each time we wanted to play, we never had the same people around. I have folders full of characters from &quot;one-shots&quot; that never went anywhere because the same group didn't show up, or we didn't have the books, or just didn't feel like playing that game that week.<br /> <br /> So, yeah... a great number of our games last 1-2 sessions. A good number of them last 8 or so sessions, but that may take a year or so to get through and we never really come to an end of a story as it just peters out, and a few rare games last many many years, but often don't follow the same characters in the same setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T23:08:54-07:00","id":244565,"title":"","content":"The longest game I've ever been in lasted eight sessions.<br /> <br /> ...I hate my group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T14:29:59-07:00","id":244997,"title":"","content":"This has been interesting. Until last year, I had never been in a game that didn't meet at least once a week. Some games I have been in have met 2 or 3 times a week. I've never understood a one shot game. I've also was wondering how much advancement do your characters get. Mine are usually never where I want them to be. The most I ever had a character advance in a White Wolf game was in a VtM game, (the 4 plus year one), my character had well over 400 Exp. and was developing nicely. Also, how many games do you play at one time. About 15 years ago I was in a game every night of the week for about a year. It was different games with different people in each with a few people overlapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T20:07:31-07:00","id":245149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/242680-how-long-have-your-games-lasted?p=244997#post244997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has been interesting. Until last year, I had never been in a game that didn't meet at least once a week. Some games I have been in have met 2 or 3 times a week. I've never understood a one shot game. I've also was wondering how much advancement do your characters get. Mine are usually never where I want them to be. The most I ever had a character advance in a White Wolf game was in a VtM game, (the 4 plus year one), my character had well over 400 Exp. and was developing nicely. Also, how many games do you play at one time. About 15 years ago I was in a game every night of the week for about a year. It was different games with different people in each with a few people overlapping.</div> </div> </div> </div>When my friends and I were in our later years of High School (mid 1990s), we had a &quot;Summer of Fun&quot;, where we gamed every day and night for 3 months... At the time, Domino's would award you a free order every 100th order... we hit that twice that Summer. Once school/college/jobs picked back up, that was it... and we were back to once a week/month again. We would often do a game once a week, on a Sunday, or a day after school where we would meet at Taco Bell, or Burger King, or something, and game for many hours (getting kicked out and moving from fast-food restaurant after restaurant as Managers didn't like us &quot;loitering&quot;, even though we continued to buy food.)<br /> <br /> College had a &quot;gaming club night&quot;, where we would often play one game a week, but swap games every other week (L5R one week, Deadlands the next, etc.)<br /> <br /> As folks moved away and jobs/families occupied more and more time, or put people on difficult schedules, trying to get ANYONE on the same repetitive night was impossible. To this day we have to work damned hard to get the same group of 5 together for the same game. Having a gaming day/night is an actual event, either requiring driving 60+ minutes to the location, and/or planning a week+ in advance to see who can attend and figuring out what the game will look like for the GM that night.<br /> Some happen semi-spontaneously when a few of us are hanging out at someone's house, and we have someone to run a game, two others there, and a phonecall made to drag another into a game (&quot;Hey, we're playing Star Wars tonight! Come on over!&quot;)<br /> <br /> As for character advancement... shit... we don't really keep track of our XP that way (not with a log, or anything) and few of our games last long enough for us to advance. Hell, to be brutally honest, up until a friend's recent game, we've never played a Werewolf: the Apocalypse game long enough to even deal with Rank Challenges, or going up in Rank (and we played that a LOT back in the day!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T11:11:12-07:00","id":245471,"title":"","content":"Games I've played in and run have covered pretty much the entire spectrum. I've had plenty only make it to one or two sessions, several campaigns run to completion in eight months to a year, and in probably my longest case a Changeling LARP that went about two years or so. One shots are frankly becoming the more viable option as adult schedules become less amenable to regular gaming, though the definition of a &quot;one shot&quot; in my group usually still means 2-3 sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T05:09:39-07:00","id":250668,"title":"","content":"The longest chronicle/campaign I\u00b4ve run has lasted for about a year, sometimes we didn\u00b4t play more than one time a month though. Usually I play in one-shots, games for a couple of sessions or mini-campaigns/chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1298-the-chronicler","name":"The Chronicler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:32:45-07:00","id":250749,"title":"","content":"I ran a World of Synnibarr (most broken game ever made) campaign that lasted 3 years with the same 5 people playing once a week. Now our group of 3 tends to make a 1 to 2 year run per campaign before switching to a new GM/ game which is either cWOD or Warhammer Fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],